From 4b7c86331598e35d71bc7eb2550da8a2062a848b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:44:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 054/122] To R2000 as AutoCAD: gradient hatches solid in the
 first color, MTEXT \P

Against AutoCAD's own R2000 save of the same drawings (sample_AC1015,
example_2000):
- gradient HATCHes (R2004+) become solid fills of the first gradient color
  (R2000 has no gradients; the entity stayed ByLayer).
- MTEXT line breaks (LF, in sample_AC1018..AC1032) are written as \P in
  DWG and DXF, as AutoCAD does; DXF had them as ^J, kept as text by DXF
  readers (dwg_fixup_mtext_linebreaks).
Now example_2004..2018 written as R2000, directly or via DXF, equal AutoCAD's
R2000 save in all 222 entities; over both groups 3258 of 3405 entities are
equal, the rest are AutoCAD's renumbered handles and anonymous blocks, R14
lacking lineweights, and three conversions not done (stacked fraction
codes, dynamic block references, fit-point splines to control points).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
